ML-KEM-1024 (FIPS 203) — vendored reference implementation

Source:   https://github.com/pq-crystals/kyber, ref/
Commit:   3edd5af5991927164edd4aacebfcbee00b8064e7 (2026-08-02)
License:  CC0 (public domain) or Apache-2.0, see LICENSE. Both allow
          commercial use and sale. We take it under Apache-2.0, matching
          the repository.

All files are byte-for-byte copies of ref/. The parameter set is chosen
by ../pq_mlkem1024.c, which builds them as one translation unit with
KYBER_K = 4 (ML-KEM-1024), renames randombytes (only the non-derand entry
points use it, and the API never calls those), and adds the FIPS 203
section 7.2 / 7.3 input checks. Symbols are namespaced by the reference
itself (pqcrystals_kyber1024_ref_*, pqcrystals_kyber_fips202_ref_*).
Not copied: randombytes.c, the test, KAT and benchmark programs, avx2/.

libc: indcpa.c, kem.c and symmetric-shake.c include <string.h>
(memcpy/memset).

Checked against NIST ACVP (ACVP-Server commit 975de31e) keyGen,
encapsulation, decapsulation and key-check vectors: ../test_pq_matrix.c.
